    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the `frai gate init --ci` bug. The issue was in how the `frai` CLI passed options to the `frai-gate` subcommand.\n\n**The Problem:**\nThe `gate` command wasn't receiving the `--ci` flag because commander was parsing global options at the main program level before delegating to the subcommand.\n\n**The Solution:**\nI made two changes to `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:\n\n1. **Added `.enablePositionalOptions()` to the main program** (line 603) - This tells commander to treat options after subcommands as positional arguments that can be passed through.\n\n2. **Changed `.allowUnknownOption(true)` to `.passThroughOptions()` on the gate command** (line 741) - This ensures all options, including flags like `--ci`, are passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI without being parsed by the main program.\n\n**Verification:**\nI tested the fix in a test directory and confirmed that running `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and is ready to use.",
